[size=7][b]FrameUI[/b][/size]
[size=5][b]Your world deserves an entrance.[/b][/size]

[b]50 animations  ·  10 ready-made designs  ·  Connected browser editor[/b]
Turn the moments between places into part of your server's identity.

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/effects/][b]Explore all 60 effects[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://frameui.despical.dev/][b]Open the FrameUI Studio[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/][b]Read the documentation[/b][/url][/center]

Welcome players through a field of stars. Travel through a portal into another world. Give your lobby a clean, branded introduction. [b]FrameUI lets you design the transition, choose when it appears and make it feel at home on your server.[/b]

Start with a bundled effect, make it your own in Studio, then save it to the server. Colors, captions, images, layout, loading indicators and timing stay under your control.

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]An entrance for every atmosphere.[/b][/size][/center]

Subtle fades, clean wipes, spirals, portals, starfields and auroras: choose from [b]50 animation templates[/b] before you begin customizing. Keep the movement understated or give a special destination a more expressive arrival.

[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/frameui/storefront/motion-v5.webp[/img]
[/center]

[b]Set the pace.[/b] Adjust the entrance, hold and exit. Change the color palette, tune the ambient motion and choose the indicator that fits the design. Every template is a starting point for your own variation.

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/effects/][b]Explore the complete effect gallery →[/b][/url]

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]A complete look. Your finishing touch.[/b][/size][/center]

Want a finished starting point? The [b]10 bundled presets[/b] bring captions, indicators and visual styling together. Choose a clean loader, the FrameUI Signature, Cherry Valley, Nether Forge or another ready-made design, then adapt it to your server.

[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/frameui/storefront/themes-v5.webp[/img]
[/center]

[b]Bring your own identity.[/b] Add a PNG logo or background, write a welcome caption and position the screen elements. Change a bundled design without losing the original: your edited version becomes a custom effect in [b]My Effects[/b].

[b]Keep it reusable.[/b] Export an effect ZIP from Studio for manual installation, or import and save through your personal server connection.

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]See your idea while you shape it.[/b][/size][/center]

Open the browser editor, choose a design and work directly on the preview. [b]Move and resize elements on the canvas[/b], adjust the palette and timing, and see how the pieces fit together before testing the finished effect in Minecraft.

[center][img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/frameui/storefront/studio-v5.webp[/img]
[size=3]The Studio interface with a full Signature transition. Previews on this page are Studio renders.[/size][/center]

[list=1][*][b]Open your connection.[/b] Run /frameui editor in Minecraft and follow your personal link.
[*][b]Make the design yours.[/b] Choose a template, adjust its colors, add an image or caption and set the layout.
[*][b]Choose when it plays.[/b] Select automatic events in Studio's When to play controls.
[*][b]Send it to the server.[/b] Import a new custom effect or save changes to an existing one.[/list=1]

[b]No account is required.[/b] Standalone Studio also works without a server connection and can export a ZIP. Personal server links expire and should stay private.

[url=https://frameui.despical.dev/][b]Open the FrameUI Studio[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui-studio/][b]Follow the Studio guide[/b][/url]

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]Your effect. Your rules.[/b][/size]

[img]https://docs.despical.dev/images/frameui/storefront/playback-v4.webp[/img][/center]

[b]Welcome a player.[/b] Bind an effect to joining the server. [b]Mark a journey.[/b] Play a transition after a teleport or world change. Use different looks for different places, players and travel routes.

Permissions, source and destination worlds, game modes, teleport causes, distance, time, weather and cooldowns determine which effects are eligible. [b]Priorities choose the preferred candidates; weights vary the result between equally prioritized designs.[/b]

Automatic effect playback is off until you configure it. Effects begin after the client world and resource pack are available; Minecraft controls its own startup and terrain-download screens.

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/automatic-playback/][b]Automatic playback guide[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/filters/][b]Filters and effect selection[/b][/url]

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]Connected to the way you already play.[/b][/size][/center]

Optional hooks connect FrameUI to the homes, warps, portals, towns, lands and islands your server uses.

[list][*][b]Homes, warps and travel:[/b] EssentialsX, HuskHomes, CMI and BetterRTP.
[*][b]Worlds and portals:[/b] Multiverse-Core and Multiverse-Portals.
[*][b]Towns, claims and islands:[/b] Towny, Lands and SuperiorSkyblock2.
[*][b]Dynamic captions:[/b] PlaceholderAPI can expand caption text.[/list]

Install only the integrations you need. Travel effects require a real local teleport. For a proxy transfer, use a Join binding on the destination server.

[b]Speak your community's language.[/b] Choose from [b]28 bundled languages[/b] for plugin messages and Studio controls. Customize chat panels and MiniMessage text while preserving command permissions and your own messages.

[spoiler=The 28 bundled languages]
English, Spanish, Russian, German, French, Portuguese, Polish, Turkish, Chinese, Indonesian, Italian, Vietnamese, Dutch, Korean, Czech, Thai, Hungarian, Arabic, Japanese, Ukrainian, Swedish, Danish, Romanian, Slovak, Hebrew, Lithuanian, Malay and Tamil.
[/spoiler]

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/integrations/][b]Integration setup[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/configuration/messages/][b]Messages and languages[/b][/url]

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]Install. Preview. Make it yours.[/b][/size][/center]

[b]Requirements:[/b] Java 25 or newer on the server, Paper 1.21.11 through 26.3 (both endpoints included), and a matching vanilla first-person Minecraft Java Edition client in that range with the required FrameUI resource pack accepted. Bedrock/Geyser, rendering mods and Folia are not qualified.

[list=1][*]Place [b]FrameUI.jar[/b] in your server's plugins folder and restart.
[*]Join and accept the required resource pack.
[*]Run [b]/frameui effects[/b] to find a design.
[*]Try [b]/frameui preview matrix[/b], then use [b]/frameui stop[/b] to close it.
[*]Open [b]/frameui editor[/b] and configure your first custom effect.[/list=1]

The default setup handles Studio and pack delivery over outbound HTTPS. No inbound port or account is needed. Automatic effect playback starts when you enable the event bindings.

[spoiler=Commands and permissions]
[b]/frameui[/b] — show the available commands.
[b]/frameui effects[/b] — browse animations, presets and custom effects.
[b]/frameui preview <effect>[/b] — preview a selected effect; random chooses an eligible design.
[b]/frameui stop[/b] — close your current or pending effect.
[b]/frameui editor[/b] — open your personal editor connection.
[b]/frameui status[/b] — inspect loaded effects and current playback.
[b]/frameui reload[/b] — validate and apply configuration changes.

Each command has its own permission. Help and stop default to everyone; management commands default to operators. [url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/commands/]Read the complete command and permission reference.[/url]
[/spoiler]

[url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/getting-started/][b]Full installation guide[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://docs.despical.dev/frameui/troubleshooting/][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/url]

[hr]

[center]
[size=6][b]A clearer picture of how FrameUI is used.[/b][/size][/center]

FrameUI reports [b]aggregate usage statistics[/b] through bStats. These help show adoption and version usage. Server owners can disable reporting by setting [b]enabled: false[/b] in [b]plugins/bStats/config.yml[/b] and restarting. FrameUI adds no custom charts or player identifiers.

[center][url=https://bstats.org/plugin/bukkit/FrameUI%20by%20Despical/34988][img]https://bstats.org/signatures/bukkit/FrameUI%20by%20Despical.svg[/img][/url][/center]

